1 finding(s): 1 to consider; 0 on their lines. Reply in a comment's thread to answer it.

### Outside the diff

- 🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: Picking the folder the workspace already points at still toasts "now points to the new folder" (confidence high)** (`apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx:167`): `relocateWorkspace` now returns early with the unchanged entry when the chosen path is the current one (`relocate.ts:43`). The result is still `{ ok: true }`, so `onRelocated` here and the dialog's `onRelocated(result)` (`workspace-dialog.tsx:145`) show `folderChanged`: "Done. {name} now points to the new folder." The picker opens at `dirname(entry.path)`, so picking the same folder is easy, and the user is told something changed when nothing did. Consider distinguishing the no-op, or wording the toast so it is true in both cases.

### Summary

The change closes most of the earlier threads. The deferred color upgrade now has its own marker. It writes only if the folder still holds the old Default and rose, otherwise the folder wins, and an explicit edit clears it. `pendingInit` workspaces can be relocated. A same-folder pick returns early. Rejected create, edit and relocate calls show an "outcome unknown" message. I found one small issue: picking the folder a workspace already points at still toasts "now points to the new folder". Two earlier threads stay open: `pendingInit` relocation to a folder holding another workspace's id is still refused as `different`, and the capture drop on relocating the active workspace is untouched.

